# PenguinCode dependency lock source.
#
# NOTE: this is a secondary artifact for pip-audit/dependency-scan tooling.
# The package is actually installed via `pip install -e '.[dev]'` (see
# Dockerfile.server and .github/workflows/docker-build.yml's test-penguincode
# job), so pyproject.toml's `dependencies`/`optional-dependencies.dev` lists
# are the real, enforced pin set and are kept in exact `==` sync with this
# file. Regenerate requirements.txt whenever pyproject.toml's dependency pins
# change:
#   uv pip compile --python-version 3.13 --generate-hashes \
#     services/penguincode/requirements.in -o services/penguincode/requirements.txt

